                  "explanation": "Across Blue Zones, the daily legume intake hovers around **1 cup of cooked beans/lentils (~180 g)**. The Darmadi-Blackberry data suggested that **each additional 20 g** of daily legumes reduces all-cause mortality by **8%** — so a cup gets you most of the achievable benefit. Higher intakes are common (Nicoyans often eat ~1.5 cups), but the practical Blue Zone target is **1 cup of cooked legumes daily**, every day, in any form.",
